MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The memory card and reader felt useful because my recent Canon camcorder gives me a concrete reason to record and transfer footage, provided the card is compatible.",
    "The Echo Show felt like a natural addition to my Fire TV and security setup because its screen could offer a convenient way to view compatible cameras and use Alexa controls."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The earbuds, charging cables, and drone holder lacked a clear connection to something I currently need; owning home electronics does not mean I need phone or drone accessories.",
    "More security cameras fit my interests but did not automatically feel worth choosing now: I recently added a Blink camera, have no stated need for three more indoor cameras, and would need to check wiring before considering the Ring doorbell."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat a broad interest in electronics as a reason to suggest accessories without evidence that I own the devices they support.",
    "My Fire TV and security purchases seemed to lead to a broad range of Alexa products, even when their purpose, such as in-car voice control, did not match my current home-focused needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases suggest that useful additions to equipment I already have can matter more than buying another device that serves a need I just addressed.",
    "Compatibility and a specific use matter to me: the memory card needs to work with my camcorder, camera viewing needs to work with the Echo Show, and the doorbell needs suitable wiring."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in home video and security but sometimes confused related gadgets with useful next additions to my existing setup."
}
